            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe current highlighting ([regular and when indent is \"off\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9618cf56e76cc0caab54ad60116a8d72f99d7b3b/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L58-L62)) provides enough information to be useful. On the other hand, rainbow indent levels are mostly useful if there can be several of them shown, while 'mini.indentscope' has (and will have) only one shown at a time.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
